          dusty, and their outlets are often shared or protected in ways a treadmill motor dislikes. A
          lot of buyers put a treadmill there anyway and only discover the problem when they make a
          warranty claim. So this page starts where a garage buyer should: with what each maker's
          manual actually says about garages, temperature and humidity. The picks follow from that,
          and so does the advice on cold starts, rust, dust and power that applies to whatever you buy.
        </p>

